Three points, no more. 1) Invocation contract: you must implement an execution adapter (dispatcher), logically and ideally physically separate from the core domain. It reads a single JSON object from stdin, inspects the 'action' field to route to the correct core function, then prints the result to stdout matching the per-feature output contract. All policy durations in inputs are in seconds; all time points are epoch milliseconds. The adapter contains zero business logic — every numeric result and boolean decision is delegated to the core domain. There is no argv-based CLI to design; stdin JSON in, observable stdout out. 2) Harness contract: deliver a bash test harness at rcb_tests/test.sh. It accepts --cases-dir <subdir> (default: test_cases) pointing at a directory of *.json case files under rcb_tests/. For each case file it runs every case in the 'cases' array against the dispatcher, writing raw stdout (no PASS/FAIL metadata) to rcb_tests/stdout/<cases-dir>/{filename_stem}@{case_index_zero_padded_3}.txt — e.g. rcb_tests/stdout/public_test_cases/feature1_next_retry_at@000.txt. Namespaced by <cases-dir> so directories never overwrite each other. 'bash rcb_tests/test.sh' runs the full suite with the default dir. 3) Example case, from feature2_1_deduplication:
{
  "description": "By default deduplication is on: the backend (here the error-trigger notifier) is invoked only on the first occurrence of each identifier within a run, even though the per-identifier counter keeps incrementing on every occurrence.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "enable": [
          "trigger"
        ],
        "triggers": [
          {
            "package": "acme/orm",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/orm/1234",
            "message": "this is deprecated %s %d",
            "args": [
              "foo",
              1234
            ]
          },
          {
            "package": "acme/orm",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/orm/1234",
            "message": "this is deprecated %s %d",
            "args": [
              "foo",
              1234
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "event=deprecation_notice\nbackend=trigger_error\nmessage=this is deprecated foo 1234\npackage=acme/orm\nlink=https://dep.example.com/orm/1234\nunique_count=2\ncount[https://dep.example.com/orm/1234]=2\n"
    }
  ]
}
The 'input' object is what your adapter parses from stdin; the 'expected_output' string is the exact raw stdout. Public test cases exist, one file per feature — ask by feature name and I will hand over the full JSON.

Two named artifacts, both delivered verbatim. feature1_1_default_noop:
{
  "description": "When no activation mode has been selected, the manager is a complete no-op: triggering a deprecation neither records a counter nor notifies any backend. The unique total stays zero and no identifiers are tracked.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "triggers": [
          {
            "package": "acme/orm",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/orm/1234",
            "message": "a deprecated call"
