Both artifacts, verbatim. feature5_1_ignore_identifier:
{
  "description": "An identifier can be suppressed entirely. A suppressed identifier is skipped before any counting takes place: it is neither counted nor sent to any backend, as if it had never been triggered.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "enable": [
          "trigger"
        ],
        "ignore_links": [
          "https://dep.example.com/orm/1234"
        ],
        "triggers": [
          {
            "package": "acme/orm",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/orm/1234",
            "message": "this is deprecated %s %d",
            "args": [
              "foo",
              1234
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "unique_count=0\ntracked=(none)\n"
    }
  ]
}
feature5_2_ignore_package:
{
  "description": "A whole package can be silenced from backend notifications. Deprecations from a silenced package are still counted (tracking is unaffected), but no backend notification is emitted for them.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "enable": [
          "trigger"
        ],
        "ignore_packages": [
          "acme/orm"
        ],
        "triggers": [
          {
            "package": "acme/orm",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/orm/1234",
            "message": "this is deprecated %s %d",
            "args": [
              "foo",
              1234
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "unique_count=1\ncount[https://dep.example.com/orm/1234]=1\n"
    }
  ]
}
The asymmetry is the whole point of this pair: ignore_links kills counting entirely (tracked=(none)), while ignore_packages only mutes notification — counting proceeds untouched. Four feature files remain: feature6_env_activation, feature7_called_from_outside, feature8_disable_reset — plus feature2_1_deduplication if you skipped it earlier. Name the next one.

Both artifacts, verbatim. feature6_env_activation:
{
  "description": "Activation can be driven by an environment selector instead of explicit calls. The selector value 'track' enables counting only; 'trigger' enables the error-trigger backend; any other/absent value leaves the manager a no-op.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": {
        "env": "track",
        "triggers": [
          {
            "package": "acme/foo",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/foo/1",
            "message": "message"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "unique_count=1\ncount[https://dep.example.com/foo/1]=1\n"
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "env": "trigger",
        "triggers": [
          {
            "package": "acme/foo",
            "link": "https://dep.example.com/foo/1",
            "message": "message"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": "event=deprecation_notice\nbackend=trigger_error\nmessage=message\npackage=acme/foo\nlink=https://dep.example.com/foo/1\nunique_count=1\ncount[https://dep.example.com/foo/1]=1\n"
    }
